# 15. Power / Interest Analysis

The following stakeholder classification will be used to determine the level of engagement required.

| Category                     | Stakeholder Groups                                       | Engagement Approach |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| High Power / High Interest   | Product Owner, HR Manager, Operations Manager, Nida Khan | Manage Closely      |
| High Power / Lower Interest  | Senior Management                                        | Keep Satisfied      |
| Lower Power / High Interest  | HR Users, Operations Users, Recruitment Users            | Keep Informed       |
| Medium Power / High Interest | Finance Manager, Recruitment Lead                        | Keep Engaged        |

---

# 16. Stakeholder Engagement Strategy

## Manage Closely

Stakeholders in this category should be actively involved in:

* Requirement decisions
* Business-rule validation
* Sprint Reviews
* UAT
* Scope decisions
* Acceptance activities

## Keep Satisfied

Stakeholders should receive concise management-level information including:

* Project progress
* Major risks
* KPI requirements
* Milestones
* Release status

## Keep Engaged

Stakeholders should be involved when requirements or functionality directly affect their business area.

## Keep Informed

End users should receive:

* Process information
* UAT schedules
* Release information
* Training information
* Known changes affecting their workflows

