# 19. Stakeholder Management Principles

The following principles will be applied throughout the project:

1. Business requirements will be validated with the appropriate process owner.
2. Technical decisions will consider documented business requirements.
3. Stakeholder decisions affecting scope will be recorded.
4. Requirement changes will be reflected in the product backlog and traceability documentation.
5. UAT participants will represent the users of the affected business process.
6. Stakeholder feedback will be reviewed during Sprint Reviews and requirement refinement.
7. Conflicting requirements will be documented and escalated to the Product Owner for prioritization.

---

# 20. Review and Maintenance

This Stakeholder Register will be reviewed:

* At project initiation
* During major scope changes
* When a new stakeholder is identified
* Before major UAT cycles
* Before project closure

Any material stakeholder changes will be reflected in the document version history.

